    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Mia, how do plants make their food?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "🌱",
          "label": "Plant"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "🍽️",
          "label": "Food?"
        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Plants don't eat like we do. They make their own food, right inside their leaves!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🍃",
        "text": "Food made in leaves",
        "cue": "leaves",
        "sub": "Their very own food",
        "sub_cue": "own"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What do they need to make it?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Just three things: sunlight, water, and air.",
      "punch": "three",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Plant recipe",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "☀️",
            "label": "Sunlight",
            "cue": "sunlight"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💧",
            "label": "Water",
            "cue": "water"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💨",
            "label": "Air",
            "cue": "air"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "The roots drink water from the soil, and it travels up the stem to the leaves.",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "Water's trip",
        "traveler": "💧",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🌱",
            "label": "Roots drink",
            "cue": "roots"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🌿",
            "label": "Up the stem",
            "cue": "stem"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🍃",
            "label": "To the leaves",
            "cue": "leaves"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And how do they get the air?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Leaves have tiny holes, too small to see. They take in a gas from the air called carbon dioxide.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🍃",
        "text": "Tiny holes take in air",
        "cue": "holes",
        "sub": "Carbon dioxide",
        "sub_cue": "carbon"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "The green stuff in the leaves catches sunlight, and uses it to turn the water and air into sugar. That's plant food!",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Making food",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "☀️",
            "label": "Catch the sunlight",
            "cue": "catches"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔄",
            "label": "Turn water and air...",
            "cue": "turn"
          },
          {
            "icon": "img:General_items/Servier/sugar",
            "label": "...into sugar food!",
            "cue": "sugar"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Plants make sugar? Cool! Does it have a name?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "It's called photosynthesis. And there's a bonus: plants give out oxygen, the air we need to breathe!",
      "punch": "oxygen",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌳",
        "text": "Plants give us oxygen",
        "cue": "oxygen",
        "sub": "Say: FOH-toh-SIN-thuh-sis",
        "sub_cue": "photosynthesis"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So sunlight, water and air make plant food, and we get oxygen. Thanks, plants!",
      "board": {
        "type": "summary",
        "rows": [
          {
            "icon": "☀️",
            "text": "Sunlight",
            "cue": "sunlight"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💧",
            "text": "Water",
